From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 18:58:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ports/arkweb: JS dialogs (alert/confirm/prompt)

Bridge Servo's show_embedder_control(EmbedderControl::SimpleDialog) to
ACE's OnAlertDialogByJS/OnConfirmDialogByJS/OnPromptDialogByJS. The
(!Send) SimpleDialog is parked on the servo thread keyed by an id; ACE
returns the user's choice through an NWebJSDialogResult that routes back
as an Action (resolve_js_dialog) to confirm/dismiss the parked dialog.
When no ACE handler takes the dialog, the shim resolves it locally so the
page's script is never blocked (alert acknowledges, confirm/prompt cancel).

ACE marshals the dialog callbacks to its JS thread (PostSyncTask), so
calling them from the servo thread is safe.

Also drop the now-unused BuiltWebView.rendering_context field (its only
reader was removed by the resize fix; the delegate and painter hold their
own clones).

For the handled path, add conftest helpers dump_layout()/find_center()
(and a `dump` fixture) that read the ArkUI component tree via
`uitest dumpLayout`, so tests can tap ArkUI components (e.g. an
AlertDialog's buttons) by looked-up bounds instead of hard-coded
coordinates. test_dialogs.py covers both paths: unhandled (alert()
resolves and the script continues, confirm() -> false, prompt() -> null)
and handled (the arkweb-test DialogPage shows a real AlertDialog whose
OK/Cancel button is found via the layout dump and tapped, asserting the
returned value). The handled tests skip if the DialogPage is not
installed.

Verified on rk3568: 6 dialog tests pass (3 unhandled + 3 handled).

Validation: Test by running uv run ports/arkweb/tools/test_dialogs.py on a device.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; implementation and on-device testing)
